OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788899632
OL,1,Vk4                               G4/20
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGCISKEI LEADER
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGDEFIES ANC
OL,4,D
OL,5, Brigadier Oupa Gqozo says he will not
OL,6, resign and will not accede to demands
OL,7, for a referendum following the massacre
OL,8, of 28 ANC protesters yesterday.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FHe told the BBC that his troops opened
OL,11,Ffire after one of them was shot dead,
OL,12,Fand had acted with some restraint.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FMeanwhile, the South African Law and
OL,15,FOrder Ministry has criticised the ANC
OL,16,Ffor its part in the Siskei massacre.
OL,18,FThe demonstration was not a spontaneous
OL,19,Foutburst of democratic rage but part of
OL,20,Fthe ANC's programme of action, it said.
OL,21,F
OL,22,D]F This Ceefax page is fromG08-09-92
OL,23,D] FMuch more at: teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788899632
OL,1,Vk4                               G5/20
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMANDELA DEMANDS INQUIRY
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGINTO CISKEI MASSACRE
OL,4,D
OL,5, ANC leader Nelson Mandela has called
OL,6, for a full investigation into the
OL,7, massacre of 28 protesters in the South
OL,8, African homeland of Ciskei.
OL,10,FLaying a wreath at the site of the
OL,11,Fkillings, he demanded the immediate
OL,12,Fremoval of Ciskei's leader Oupa Gqozo.
OL,14,FIn a bitter attack, Mr Mandela accused
OL,15,FPresident de Klerk of soliciting his
OL,16,Fhis cooperation "whilst he was busy
OL,17,Fpreparing for war against the people".
OL,19,FEarlier, Archbishop Desmond Tutu put a
OL,20,Fplan for a referendum to Ciskei's
OL,21,Fleadership to defuse the crisis.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG08-09-92F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788899632
OL,1,Vk4                               G6/20
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGCBI TELLS TUC PAY RISES
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGMUST BE EARNED
OL,4,D
OL,5, CBI director-general Howard Davies has
OL,6, told the TUC public sector pay should
OL,7, only rise if productivity improves.
OL,9,FIn the first speech to the TUC by an
OL,10,Femployers' leader, Mr Davies also said
OL,11,Fthat executives' pay increases should
OL,12,Fbe justified by higher performance.
OL,14,FHe called on the Government to boost
OL,15,Fthe economy with spending on transport
OL,16,Finfrastructure and construction.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FMeanwhile, he said there could be no
OL,19,Freturn to the old corporatism with big
OL,20,Fdeals between union and business
OL,21,Fleaders.
OL,23,D]FFromG08-09-92F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11807
