OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788899632
OL,1,Vk4                               G8/20
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGTWO FRENCH UN SOLDIERS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGKILLED IN SARAJEVO
OL,5, Two French UN soldiers were killed when
OL,6, a UN convoy was hit by machinegun fire
OL,7, near Sarajevo airport this evening.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FA spokesman said the convoy was hit
OL,10,Fafter a long drive from Belgrade and it
OL,11,Fwas unclear who opened fire, raising
OL,12,Fthe death toll among UN troops in
OL,13,FBosnia to four with 46 wounded.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FEarlier, Bosnian Serb leader Radovan
OL,16,FKaradzic did not make it clear whether
OL,17,Fhis forces would abide by a deadline
OL,18,Fset for UN control of heavy weapons.
OL,20,FEC peace negotiator Lord Owen is
OL,21,Fexpected to visit Sarajevo tomorrow.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG08-09-92F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11809
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788899632
OL,1,Vk4                               G9/20
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMORE ARRESTS LIKELY AFTER
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGCOUNTERFEITING RAIDS
OL,4,F
OL,5, Armed police took part in a major swoop
OL,6, against organised crime in southern
OL,7, England today; 27 people were arrested.
OL,9,FMore than #1.5m in forged currency was
OL,10,Fseized, together with forged documents,
OL,11,Fover 40 guns, plastic explosives and
OL,12,Fstolen cars.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FThe raids were the climax of a probe
OL,15,Finto a "quartermaster" service
OL,16,Fsupplying criminals with the tools of
OL,17,Ftheir trade.
OL,19,FThe raids, codenamed Mensa, involved
OL,20,Fmore than 100 police officers in Devon,
OL,21,FDorset, London and the Home Counties.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG08-09-92F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
